<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
fastdds_unicast.xml
====================
SUPERSEDED 2026-07-13: replaced by Fast-DDS Discovery Server
(ROS_DISCOVERY_SERVER, started in start_swarm_motion.sh) — this profile's
initialPeersList never specified a port, so it could only ever reach one
fixed participant slot and proved unreliable as the swarm grew. No longer
referenced by any script. Left here for reference only.
WSL2's virtual network adapter does not reliably support IPv4 UDP
multicast, which is what Fast-DDS (ROS2 Humble's default RMW) uses for
participant discovery (SPDP) out of the box. Symptom: a publisher believes
it is sending fine (its own bookkeeping shows fresh outgoing data), but a
subscriber in a different process — especially one started slightly later,
e.g. a coop_loc_* node launched after inter_drone_ranging.py — never
discovers it, silently. Confirmed via `ip maddr show lo` showing zero IPv4
multicast groups joined (only IPv6).

Fix: force discovery over unicast to a fixed localhost peer list instead
of relying on multicast announcements. Everything in this project runs on
127.0.0.1, so this is sufficient.

Usage: export FASTRTPS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE=<path to this file>
before launching any ROS2 node (source'd once in $SRC in
run_experiment_motion.sh and start_swarm_motion.sh covers the whole
pipeline). Does not affect PX4 SITL itself — the uXRCE-DDS bridge between
PX4 and ROS2 is a separate point-to-point protocol on a fixed port, not
Fast-DDS multicast discovery.
-->
<dds xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com/XMLSchemas/fastRTPS_Profiles">
    <profiles>
        <participant profile_name="unicast_discovery" is_default_profile="true">
            <rtps>
                <builtin>
                    <discovery_config>
                        <discoveryProtocol>SIMPLE</discoveryProtocol>
                    </discovery_config>
                    <metatrafficUnicastLocatorList>
                        <locator/>
                    </metatrafficUnicastLocatorList>
                    <initialPeersList>
                        <locator>
                            <udpv4>
                                <address>127.0.0.1</address>
                            </udpv4>
                        </locator>
                    </initialPeersList>
                </builtin>
            </rtps>
        </participant>
    </profiles>
</dds>
